            "id": "seed-sbma",
            "name": "South Bay Mutual Aid",
            "handle": "sbma",
            "foundedYear": 2020,
            "focusAreas": ["general", "food", "housing"],
            "description": "Neighbors helping neighbors across the South Bay: weekly grocery runs, a community fridge, and help finding housing.\n\nWe started in spring 2020, when a few of us began dropping off groceries for neighbors who couldn't leave home. Today more than forty volunteers keep things going. Every Saturday morning we pack and deliver grocery boxes to families in San José, Santa Clara and Milpitas, with rice, fresh produce, and halal and vegetarian options.\n\nThe community fridge outside the library on Alum Rock Avenue is open all day, every day. Take what you need, leave what you can. We clean it and restock it twice a day.\n\nIf you're looking for housing, our housing team can help you search listings, fill out applications, and find emergency shelter or rental assistance. We speak English, Spanish and Vietnamese.\n\nNo forms, no proof of need. Just ask.",
            "placeId": "5392171",
